NZ_CP064065.1	Protein Homology	CDS	1901673	1901966	.	-	0	ID=cds-WP_170914118.1;Parent=gene-ISO16_RS08320;Dbxref=GenBank:WP_170914118.1;Name=WP_170914118.1;Note=MftB%2C a small protein%2C is a peptide chaperone that assists the radical SAM enzyme MftC in performing two modifications to the C-terminal Val-Tyr dipeptide of the mycofactocin precursor peptide%2C MftA. MftB's role is analogous to the role of PqqD in the biosynthesis of PQQ%2C a cofactor that derives entirely from a Tyr and a Glu in the precursor PqqA.;Ontology_term=GO:0140604,GO:0042277;gbkey=CDS;gene=mftB;go_function=peptide binding|0042277||IEA;go_process=mycofactocin biosynthetic process|0140604||IEA;inference=COORDINATES: similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_016932568.1;locus_tag=ISO16_RS08320;product=mycofactocin biosynthesis chaperone MftB;protein_id=WP_170914118.1;transl_table=11
